# Runde 68: der Arbeitsordner dieser Runde (Logs der Abnahmelaeufe).
.r68/
# Round 65: the work directory of the JavaScript run. It got into the
# repository by accident in round 63 -- 32962 files, 140 MB, every one of
# them PRODUCED: `.js-work/t262` is unpacked from
# testdata/test262/test262-subset.tar.gz, `cmp/` comes from
# tools/js/compare_node.sh, the reports come from the harness. That is also
# why tools/english/check.sh counted 828 German path names: it holds every
# path that git manages against the morpheme table, and the test suite of
# TC39 is full of words like 'fall' and 'hole'.
.js-work/
.lexnum-work/

# Runde 73: der Arbeitsordner dieser Runde (Aufteilungsskripte, Logs der
# Abnahmelaeufe). NICHT ignoriert werden die HANDGESCHRIEBENEN Quellen der
# Runde -- lib/mem/, lib/math/, lib/str/core_*.fi, lib/num/core_*.fi,
# demos/kernel/kcore.fi, tools/core/ -- die gehoeren ins Repo.
.r73/

# Round 71: the work directories of this round (f32 sweeps, ABI cross check
# against GCC).
.f32work/
.abi-work/
.baseline-*.log

# Round 71: the test data of the round are PRODUCED (tools/f32data/gen.py),
# not checked in -- binary rubbish in a repository is something nobody can
# read, and a generator can be looked at.
testdata/f32/
.f32data-work/

# Round 75: the work directory of tools/extfn/run.sh (linked probe binaries,
# object files, build/link logs).
.extfn-work/
# round 76: the third party client for tools/mcserver/run.sh -- 453 MiB of
# minecraft-data, fetched on demand by the script, never committed.
tools/mcserver/node_modules/
tools/mcserver/package-lock.json
tools/mcserver/package.json

# Round 79: the work directory of tools/escape/run.sh (probe binaries and
# the two compilers' messages, which the script holds against each other).
.escape-work/
# Round 80: the work directories of the second machine (cross-compiled
# probes, the two build stages of the corpus, the ELF/relocation checks).
.a64-work/
.a64-machine/
# The hand-written A64 `strlen` of tools/aarch64/impl.s is SOURCE, in the
# same way demos/kernel/boot.s is -- it is the foreign side of the foreign
# function proof, and a code generator must not be allowed to produce it.
!tools/aarch64/impl.s
.frag-work/
tools/gc_frag/measurement-*.tsv
